@startuml
title Teacher Feature — Sequence Diagram (Specify level)
autonumber

actor Teacher
participant "Teacher Pages" as UI
participant "Teacher Access Guard" as Guard
participant "Activity Management" as Activity
participant "Guided Notes Import" as Import
participant "Google Sheets Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Google Sheets" as Sheets
participant "Round Control" as Control
participant "Foundation Lifecycle" as Lifecycle
participant "Student End Coordinator" as Coord
participant "Student Winner Resolver" as Resolver
participant "Teacher Monitor" as Monitor
participant "Answer Write-back" as WriteBack
participant "Session State Events" as Events
actor "Students (>= 2 Teams)" as Students

== Login ==
Teacher -> UI : enter password
UI -> Guard : login
Guard -> Guard : verify password hash, rate limit
Guard --> UI : teacher login credential (not readable by page scripts)

== Create activity ==
Teacher -> UI : create activity with N Teams
UI -> Guard : teacher-only request
Guard -> Guard : verify credential, origin, CSRF
Guard -> Activity : create
Activity --> UI : activity code, Team 1..N names

== Import Guided Notes ==
UI -> Guard : sheet URL
Guard -> Import : parse request
Import -> Gateway : read sheet
Gateway -> Sheets : read cells and merges
alt not shared / not found / bad URL
  Sheets --> Gateway : error
  Import --> UI : SHEET_NOT_SHARED / SHEET_NOT_FOUND / INVALID_SHEET_URL
else readable
  Sheets --> Gateway : cells
  Import -> Import : locate headers, detect groups (vertical merge),\ndetect blanks (markers), validate
  alt format invalid / duplicate numbers
    Import --> UI : SHEET_FORMAT_INVALID / duplicate number
  else ok
    Import --> UI : preview (numbers, groups, blank cells)
    Teacher -> UI : confirm
    UI -> Import : confirm
    Import -> Import : create Questions, Blanks, Groups,\nBlank Cell Mappings
  end
end

== Round control ==
Teacher -> UI : select target / next / reopen
UI -> Guard : command with expected state version
Guard -> Control : per-Session Teacher context
Control -> Lifecycle : create Waiting Round
Lifecycle -> Events : publish after commit
Events --> Students : Waiting (<= 2 s)
Teacher -> UI : start
UI -> Control : start
Control -> Lifecycle : Waiting -> Active
Lifecycle -> Events : publish after commit
Events --> Students : Active (<= 2 s)

== Monitoring ==
Students -> Students : leader submits (Student Feature)
Monitor --> UI : submitted Teams and order (<= 2 s)\n(teacher only; no drafts)
Teacher -> UI : show answers (optional)
UI -> Monitor : answers
Monitor --> UI : per-blank answers

== End round ==
Teacher -> UI : end
UI -> Control : end with expected state version
Control -> Coord : endRound(input, teacher context) (single call)
Coord -> Coord : check teacher, Session scope, round:end
Coord -> Lifecycle : end with winner resolver
Lifecycle -> Lifecycle : one write transaction
Lifecycle -> Resolver : resolve winner (same transaction)
Resolver --> Lifecycle : earliest accepted Submission or none
Lifecycle -> Lifecycle : Ended + Result (or clear old Result), commit
Lifecycle -> Events : publish after commit
Events --> Students : Ended
Coord --> Control : committed state
alt conflict (stale state or wrong phase)
  Control --> UI : conflict
  UI -> Guard : reload latest state
end
UI -> Monitor : results
Monitor --> UI : full order, winner Team and answers / no winner

== Write-back ==
Teacher -> UI : write back winners
UI -> WriteBack : build plan
WriteBack -> WriteBack : all targets with winners\n+ previously written targets now without winner (restore original)
WriteBack -> Gateway : read current target cells
Gateway -> Sheets : read
WriteBack --> UI : cells, current content, new content (marker kept + answer)
Teacher -> UI : confirm
UI -> WriteBack : confirm
WriteBack -> Gateway : re-check cells
alt any cell changed or missing
  WriteBack --> UI : conflict list, nothing written
else unchanged
  WriteBack -> Gateway : write all cells
  Gateway -> Sheets : write
  WriteBack --> UI : written
end

== CSV export ==
Teacher -> UI : export
UI -> Guard : teacher-only request
Guard --> UI : CSV (one row per Round per Team)
@enduml
